DSH video preview in the sidebar - source patch
===============================================

Makes the DSH Web sidebar preview play video files (mp4, m4v, webm, ogv, ogg,
mov, mkv) with the browser's own player, and removes the 32 MiB ceiling that
previously made `readAll` refuse the large files this workspace produces.

Target file (the built client half of the Sidebar document-preview plugin):
  node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-sidebar-documentpreview/lib/client.js
  relative to the DSH install; here that is
  /home/xiongti1/.npm/_npx/1e7f6d9597241db0/

Apply from that package directory:
  patch -p0 --dry-run < dsh-video-preview.patch   # check
  patch -p0 < dsh-video-preview.patch             # apply

What it changes
  1. createReadAllBytes(): complete-byte previews read the file in the Host's
     bounded byte windows (readBytes, 2 MiB default) and assemble them, so a
     46.9 MB mp4 previews where readAll's 32 MiB cap used to refuse it. Small
     files still cost one window; any window failure falls back to readAll, and
     an aborted read stops without a second RPC.
  2. documentFileBytes(): accepts already-native bytes, so assembly avoids a
     base64 round trip.
  3. A per-tab read-progress action plus a percentage label while bytes load.
  4. A video renderer: metadata (builtin band, bytes-complete), zh/en labels,
     and a body that mints a Blob URL and renders <video controls>. Its Blob URL
     is revoked on unmount or replacement.
  5. Existing renderers (text, Markdown, code, image, PDF, HTML) keep their
     registrations and loading modes; the "open with" menu can still switch a
     video back to plain text.

